    {
      "id": "W2",
      "severity": "important interpretation",
      "title": "Different shrinkage maps substantially change directional precision",
      "detail": "M3w shrinks residual 4x4 covariance; M5n shrinks joint 8x8 covariance before projection. These operations do not commute. A small Frobenius gap does not imply close inverse weights; generalized eigenratios are reported. Keep frozen comparison but do not interpret it as a universal intrinsic efficiency ordering."
    },
    {
      "id": "W3",
      "severity": "theory scope",
      "title": "Nonexcited-bin weights are not proven finite-sample independent",
      "detail": "Beta0 uses excited data; finite-window colored DFT ordinates can be correlated; windows overlap; fixed nl gives noisy local covariance. Separate-bin construction alone is not a proof of exact finite-sample exogeneity or exact unbiasedness. Two-stage feasible IV requires its usual asymptotic regularity conditions."
    },
    {
      "id": "W4",
      "severity": "theory scope",
      "title": "Oracle sandwich is a first-order conditional/asymptotic benchmark",
